  "gaps": [
    "The capture contains several programs (end of a health care program, the Bachelor of Arts in Homeland Security and Emergency Management, the Bachelor of Arts in Human Resources Management, and only the introduction to the Associate of Arts in Business). This ledger covers Homeland Security and Emergency Management because it is the only program whose whole section appears in the capture. Please confirm the intended program. The Human Resources Management major list uses ^ and ^^ markers whose footnotes are not in the capture.",
    "Itemized credits add up to 123 (33 Foundations + 36 major + 54 electives), not the 120 total. The capture says 3 major credits (POL 111) also satisfy Global Campus Foundations requirements. It does not say which Foundations course POL 111 replaces, so the 3-credit overlap cannot be assigned to a specific line.",
    "The Global Campus Foundations courses listed are the standard sequence. The capture says courses may be substituted, but gives no substitution rules.",
    "GEN 101 is scheduled as the first course and counts toward 3 elective credits. GEN 104 is required for bachelor students transferring in fewer than 30 credits and also counts toward 3 elective credits. Both fall inside the 54-credit elective block and are not listed separately.",
    "Residency requirement: at least 30 credits must be completed at the University. The capture does not tie this to specific courses, so no line is marked institution-only.",
    "Upper-division requirement: at least 30 upper-division credits, including 18 in the major. The capture does not define which course numbers count as upper-division.",
    "Course prerequisites for the Homeland Security major courses are not stated in the capture.",
    "Grade requirement: minimum cumulative GPA of 2.00 in all coursework attempted at the University."
  ],
